# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND on disk.
#
# `text=auto` alone only normalises what is stored in git; on checkout it still
# converts to the platform's native ending, so a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF to disk. Biome reads the bytes on disk, so
# `pnpm lint` reported format failures on whatever files git had most recently
# checked out — 10 in the main checkout, a different 20 in a fresh worktree, and
# the set moved with every branch switch. None of them were real formatting
# problems; converting line endings alone made them clean.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so the working tree matches the blobs. It is
# a repository-level fix rather than a per-machine git config, so it holds for
# every clone. Nothing here needs CRLF: there are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are excluded explicitly. `text=auto` would almost certainly detect
# these correctly on its own, but a false positive corrupts the file.
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
